   <text>
      <body>
         <div type="letter"> <div type="mainBody">
                    <p>Dear Miss Weaver: <rs type="person" key="joyc00">We</rs> are <seg xml:id="seg1" type="note-anchor">just leaving for <name type="geo" key="G_FRA_NICE">Nice</name>
                        </seg> and have had very fine weather down here. I shall write as soon as we are fixed somewhere.</p>
                    <closer>
                        <salute>Kindest regards</salute>                    	<signed>
                            <name type="person" key="joyc82">James Joyce</name>
                        </signed>
                    </closer>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div type="notes">
                <note xml:id="note1" target="#seg1" type="commentary">JJ stayed in Nice until mid-November 1922. Despite Dr Borsch’s belief that Nice’s climate would benefit JJ’s ocular problems, the climate in Nice worsened his condition, resulting in a visit to Dr Louis Colin, who used leeches to drain blood from JJ’s eye (<hi rend="italic">JJ</hi> 537-8).</note>
            </div>
      </body>
   </text>
